    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  <span class=\"learn-keyword\">Government</span> is the institution through which a society organises and manages its affairs, makes and enforces binding decisions, and maintains order. It is the oldest and most universal of all political institutions. Every organised human society — from ancient kingdoms to modern democracies — has some form of government.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Definition of Government</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Government can be defined in three main ways:</p>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li><strong>As an institution:</strong> The body of persons or agencies through which a state or political community exercises authority and performs its functions (e.g., the executive, legislature, judiciary)</li>\n  <li><strong>As a process/activity:</strong> The exercise of authority — the art of governing, making laws, and managing public affairs</li>\n  <li><strong>As a subject of study:</strong> The academic discipline that studies political institutions, processes, and behaviour (also called Political Science)</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Nature of Government</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li>Government is <strong>universal</strong> — every organized society has some form of it</li>\n  <li>Government possesses <strong>coercive power</strong> — the legal authority to compel obedience</li>\n  <li>Government is <strong>continuous</strong> — it persists even as individual leaders change</li>\n  <li>Government is <strong>territorial</strong> — it exercises authority within defined boundaries</li>\n  <li>Government claims <strong>legitimacy</strong> — its authority is accepted as right and proper by the governed</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Scope of Government</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">The scope of government refers to the range of activities and functions it performs:</p>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Scope Area</th><th>Activities</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Political/Constitutional</td><td>Law-making, maintaining order, protecting rights</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Economic</td><td>Managing national resources, taxation, regulation of trade</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Social</td><td>Education, healthcare, welfare services</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Security/Defence</td><td>Military, police, internal security</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Foreign Affairs</td><td>Diplomacy, international relations, treaties</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Importance of Government</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li>Maintains <strong>law and order</strong> — prevents chaos (Hobbes: without government, life is 'solitary, poor, nasty, brutish, and short')</li>\n  <li>Provides <strong>security</strong> — protects citizens from internal and external threats</li>\n  <li>Promotes <strong>economic development</strong> — manages resources, builds infrastructure</li>\n  <li>Ensures <strong>social welfare</strong> — provides education, healthcare, social safety nets</li>\n  <li>Protects <strong>individual rights and freedoms</strong></li>\n  <li>Represents the state in <strong>international relations</strong></li>\n  <li>Resolves <strong>disputes</strong> through a legal system</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div class=\"learn-svg-wrap\">\n  <svg class=\"learn-svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 480 190\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\">\n    <rect width=\"480\" height=\"190\" fill=\"#0f0020\" rx=\"10\"/>\n    <text x=\"240\" y=\"20\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#D4AF37\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\">Three Meanings of Government</text>\n    <rect x=\"10\" y=\"30\" width=\"140\" height=\"140\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1a0030\" stroke=\"#4B0082\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n    <text x=\"80\" y=\"52\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#D4AF37\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"bold\">INSTITUTION</text>\n    <text x=\"80\" y=\"68\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#c8c8c8\" font-size=\"8\">Bodies that exercise</text>\n    <text x=\"80\" y=\"80\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#c8c8c8\" font-size=\"8\">authority: executive,</text>\n    <text x=\"80\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#c8c8c8\" font-size=\"8\">legislature, judiciary</text>\n    <rect x=\"170\" y=\"30\" width=\"140\" height=\"140\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1a0030\" stroke=\"#28c840\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n    <text x=\"240\" y=\"52\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#28c840\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"bold\">PROCESS</text>\n    <text x=\"240\" y=\"68\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#c8c8c8\" font-size=\"8\">The art of governing;</text>\n    <text x=\"240\" y=\"80\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#c8c8c8\" font-size=\"8\">making and enforcing</text>\n    <text x=\"240\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#c8c8c8\" font-size=\"8\">laws; managing affairs</text>\n    <rect x=\"330\" y=\"30\" width=\"140\" height=\"140\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1a0030\" stroke=\"#c8b4f0\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n    <text x=\"400\" y=\"52\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#c8b4f0\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"bold\">SUBJECT</text>\n    <text x=\"400\" y=\"68\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#c8c8c8\" font-size=\"8\">Academic discipline</text>\n    <text x=\"400\" y=\"80\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#c8c8c8\" font-size=\"8\">studying political</text>\n    <text x=\"400\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#c8c8c8\" font-size=\"8\">institutions and behaviour</text>\n    <text x=\"80\" y=\"130\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#D4AF37\" font-size=\"8\">e.g., FEC, NASS</text>\n    <text x=\"240\" y=\"130\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#28c840\" font-size=\"8\">e.g., taxing, policing</text>\n    <text x=\"400\" y=\"130\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#c8b4f0\" font-size=\"8\">= Political Science</text>\n  </svg>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Government has THREE meanings: (1) as an institution (the bodies — executive, legislature, judiciary), (2) as a process (the activity of governing), and (3) as a subject of study (Political Science). WAEC commonly asks candidates to distinguish between these three meanings.\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Government is the institution through which a state exercises authority, makes laws, and manages public affairs. It is universal, coercive, continuous, and territorial. Its scope covers political, economic, social, security, and foreign affairs. Government is important for maintaining order, providing security, promoting development, and protecting rights.\n</div>\n  ",
